      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/process/Process_ActOnDecisionSupport",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "Act on decision-support guidance",
      "summary": "The point-of-care system applies one of the DAK's decision tables, published as a CPG-on-FHIR PlanDefinition, to one client ($apply) and shows the health worker what it proposes (a RequestGroup, or CDS Hooks cards).",
      "description": "The point-of-care system applies one of the DAK's decision tables, published as a CPG-on-FHIR PlanDefinition, to one client ($apply) and shows the health worker what it proposes (a RequestGroup, or CDS Hooks cards). The health worker accepts or declines each action, one tap each, and the system makes the accepted requests active in the client's CarePlan; a declined action is never written. Recording why is OPTIONAL and never blocks: Event_AddReason is a non-interrupting boundary event on the review. It happens only when the health worker taps \"add a reason\" while reviewing, starts the rationale task beside the review, and takes nothing away from it: the review completes and the care plan is updated whether or not a reason is ever recorded. Skipping is the default, because the event is absent unless chosen. The record, when made, is one FHIR Provenance. Skills: apply-decision-support, review-decision-support-guidance, record-decision-rationale, activate-accepted-guidance (package authoring-who-smart-guidelines).",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "sourcePath": "processes/content/act-on-decision-support.bpmn",
